### Bug Description
- The user reports that in OpenLayers v4.6.4, there is an unwanted gap between lines of text in a label (e.g., "4.3\nbar"), which was not present in v2.13.
- The user wants to remove or control this gap, as the previous version's (v2.13) rendering was visually preferable.

### Bug Scenario Image Analysis
- The image shows two versions of the same map label:
  - v4.6.4: There is a visible gap between the two lines of text.
  - v2.13: The lines are closer together, with no extra gap.

### Root Cause Reasoning
- The gap is likely due to the default line height or vertical spacing used when rendering multi-line text in the canvas.
- In v4.6.4, the rendering code may have introduced a default line height or padding between lines, which was not present in v2.13.
- The OpenLayers API does not expose a direct way to control this line spacing.

